  "id": "COMPOUND:699 - PROTEIN:935",
  "verbalization": "Apomorphine is linked to Dihydropteroate synthase 1 through a series of targets that share a common pathway involving the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor family. The evidence suggests that Apomorphine acts on the 5-hydroxytryptamine 3 receptor, which in turn is targeted by OPC-28326 and vernakalant, both of which ultimately affect Dihydropteroate synthase 1. This implies that Apomorphine may exert its effects through a receptor that is part of a broader signaling network influencing Dihydropteroate synthase 1. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism where Apomorphine could modulate the activity of Dihydropteroate synthase 1 via a receptor-mediated pathway, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling cascades. The evidence supports a role for Apomorphine in influencing Dihydropteroate synthase 1 through a receptor-targeted mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
